      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Code scanning can now detect AI applications and agent vulnerabilities, including indirect prompt injection (XPIA), sensitive information disclosure, excessive agency, and other AI-specific risks as coverage expands.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-code-scanning-for-ai-applications-in-public-preview",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T13:27:26.487Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Here&rsquo;s an overview of AI applications and agent vulnerabilities that are covered:",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-code-scanning-for-ai-applications-in-public-preview",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T13:27:26.487Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Indirect prompt injection is the top risk in the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-code-scanning-for-ai-applications-in-public-preview",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T13:27:26.487Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "It happens when malicious instructions are hidden in untrusted content (e.g., a file, webpage, or issue comment) that an AI agent reads.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-code-scanning-for-ai-applications-in-public-preview",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T13:27:26.487Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Sensitive information disclosure happens when an AI application or agent can access sensitive data without appropriate authorization controls, potentially exposing it to users or systems that should not have access.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-code-scanning-for-ai-applications-in-public-preview",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T13:27:26.487Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Excessive agency happens when an AI agent has more capabilities, permissions, or autonomy than its task requires, increasing the risk of unintended or high-impact actions.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-code-scanning-for-ai-applications-in-public-preview",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T13:27:26.487Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "If your organization uses GitHub Advanced Security, this detector starts scanning pull requests in repositories where code scanning and scans for AI applications are enabled.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-code-scanning-for-ai-applications-in-public-preview",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:30:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T13:27:26.487Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Code scanning for AI applications is now in public preview on github.com and requires a GitHub Advanced Security license.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-code-scanning-for-ai-applications-in-public-preview",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
